# The rejected-config tier, empty until issue #158 fills it.
#
# The tier directory exists now because the enrolment check derives tiers from
# this tree: a tier with no directory has no runner to be checked against, and
# the split this file is part of is what #158 adds cases to rather than invents.
#
# A rejected-config case is one directory holding config bytes under the
# adopter's own config filename plus one frozen expectation — never markdown, so
# the expect-marker case glob (`<tier>/docs/**/*.md`) does not reach here.
#
# `tests/rejected-config-tier.test.ts` asserts this tier holds zero case
# directories today, so the first case added turns it red rather than landing
# beside a runner that never looks at it.
